"peer_ticker": "AMD",
"peer_disclosure_id": "amd_2024_1A_D063",
"relationship": "same_topic",
"comparison": "Both NVDA and AMD disclose that reliance on customer demand estimates to forecast inventory and supply can lead to mismatches between supply and demand. NVDA broadly states that failure to estimate accurately leads to these mismatches. AMD provides more detail, noting that inventory levels are based on customer estimates which may not accurately predict future purchases, and this inaccuracy, particularly through downstream channels, can cause material adverse effects. A key difference is that AMD explicitly links this risk to inventory write-downs and gross margin impacts, referencing specific revenue decreases in its Embedded segment, whereas NVDA frames it primarily as a general operational mismatch risk.",
