"relationship": "same_topic",
"comparison": "NVDA and AVGO both identify the failure to accurately match manufacturing and supply to customer demand as a risk to operations. NVDA cites 'failure to estimate customer demand accurately' leading to supply-demand mismatches. AVGO cites 'failure to adjust our manufacturing and supply chain to accurately meet customer demand' as a risk that could adversely affect results of operations. Both companies emphasize the operational consequence (mismatch/financial impact) of inaccurate demand alignment.",
