"peer_disclosure_id": "qcom_2024_1A_D039",
"relationship": "same_topic",
"comparison": "Both NVDA and QCOM discuss the risk that manufacturing and supply orders based on demand forecasts may not align with actual customer needs, leading to negative operational impacts. NVDA warns that failure to estimate demand leads to mismatches. QCOM elaborates that placing orders based on forecasts (including customer forecasts) that are not covered by binding commitments can result in excess/obsolete inventory or reserve charges, negatively impacting results of operations. QCOM also notes that customer inventory buildups (overestimating demand) can reduce future purchases, a specific dynamic of demand estimation error.",
