"relationship": "same_topic",
"comparison": "Both NVDA and MU highlight the risk of failing to accurately predict or respond to changes in customer demand, which negatively impacts financial performance. NVDA states that failure to estimate demand accurately leads to supply-demand mismatches. MU states that the inability to predict or quickly respond to changes in customer demand could negatively impact gross margin. While NVDA focuses on the supply side mismatch, MU focuses on the responsiveness to demand trends and the direct impact on gross margin, but both address the core risk of demand estimation failure.",
